// dsv4-session-run.bml -- ask a Form-native DeepSeek-V4 session through the model session door: open, generate, how it ended, release.
//
//   echo '{"dry":1}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-session-run.bml    the plan from the header alone: the chat-templated prompt ids, the capacity and the position limit (2047), the lease the open would ask, the seal sidecar, the
//                                                              driver's gaps, the machine. Opens nothing, maps nothing, takes no lease, writes no row. Empty stdin and {} do the same: THE DEFAULT IS THE PLAN.
//   echo '{"go":1,"prompt":"The capital of France is","tokens":24}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-session-run.bml
//                                                              THE ASK. Not run by the session that wrote it: it asks for the lead's go. It is the Qwen session's three calls (fcms-open-reserved, fcms-generate,
//                                                              fcms-release-ok?) over the DeepSeek seat: the admission queue and the seal, the governor's lease, the routed-arena open and prefill, the greedy walk to a
//                                                              named ending, the release. It prints the stage lines of the open, then one line (status, reason, the usage line: prompt_tokens, generated_tokens, ending,
//                                                              position_limit; released; wall ms) and the text, and appends one row to receipts/dsv4-session-runs.jsonl.
//
// stdin, one JSON line, all optional: go, dry, file (the IQ2XXS build by default), prompt, tokens (24), receipt. The ask needs the file's seal sidecar (<file>.form-seal: "qaf-seal1:<size>:<sha256>") and no other model door
// resident. Check the machine first: ./fkwu observe/memory-governor-run.bml </dev/null must show room. Every definition is form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-session-ask.bml's, read there and held by its bands. Exit: 0 for an answered
// ask with every handle released, 1 otherwise.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-session-ask.bml
section [form.bml] {
 dsa-main();
}
